### 2. AVL Tree Construction (Bulk Loading / Sorting)

* **Naive Method:** Inserting N items one-by-one into an empty AVL tree takes **O(N log N)** time.
* **Optimal Method:** If you already have a **sorted array** of N elements, you can build a perfectly balanced AVL tree in **O(N)** time using a divide-and-conquer strategy (picking the middle element as root recursively), without executing any rotations.

---

### 3. Rotations Under the Hood: Pointer Swaps

Rotations take **O(1) constant time** because they only involve reassigning 3 to 4 pointers.

For a **Single Right Rotation (LL Case)** on node `Z` with left child `Y`:

1. `Y` becomes the new root of this subtree.
2. `Y`'s right child (`T2`) is moved to become `Z`'s left child.
3. `Z` becomes `Y`'s right child.
4. Heights of `Z` and `Y` are recalculated.

