### 5. Augmenting AVL Trees (Order-Statistic Trees)

You can store extra metadata inside each AVL node—for example, the **Size of the Subtree** rooted at that node (`subtree_size`).

By updating this count during rotations:

* You can find the **k-th smallest element** in **O(log N)** time.
* You can find the **rank of any element** in **O(log N)** time.
